#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139375} :activity/id #uuid "89a1c0b6-a897-5db4-bd62-c855d5db6af2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050363 :topic/id #uuid "42e7a396-f7f5-5ef7-82f9-ae4f6cfc0ca0" :topic/math-academy-id 2233} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139375 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139599 :tutorial/content "We can use unit conversions to convert from one set of units to another.\n\nFor instance, the speed of sound is approximately $0.34$ kilometers per second. What is this in meters per second? We can find out using the following two steps.\n\n**Step 1: Create a conversion formula.**\n\nWe are given the units\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nand we want to convert this into\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nTo figure out what we need to multiply by, we can set up an equation to help us:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{s}\\cdot\\, \\dfrac{?}{?} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nWe want to replace $\\textrm{km}$ with $\\textrm{m}$. To get rid of $\\textrm{km}$, we can put $\\textrm{km}$ in the denominator so that it cancels out:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\dfrac{\\cancel{\\textrm{km}}}{s}\\cdot \\dfrac{?}{\\cancel{\\textrm{km}}} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nThen, to introduce $\\textrm{m}$, we can put $\\textrm{m}$ in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\dfrac{\\cancel{\\textrm{km}}}{s}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\cancel{\\textrm{km}}} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nSo, our conversion formula is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{s}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{km}} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\n**Step 2: Use the conversion formula.**\n\nNow that we have our conversion formula, we need to determine the correct numbers to use, and apply it.\n\n- The speed that we wish to convert is $0.34 \\, \\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{\\textrm{s}}$.\n- There are $1\\,000$ meters per kilometer.\n\nApplying our conversion formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.34\\frac{km}{s} &= 0.34\\frac{km}{s} \\cdot 1000\\frac{m}{km} \\\\\n&= (0.34 \\cdot 1000)\\frac{km}{s} \\cdot \\frac{m}{km} \\\\\n&= 340\\frac{m}{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the speed of sound is $340$ meters per second." :tutorial/id #uuid "d1f56c71-9cb3-5a5b-881c-bfbad588ca7f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1404 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "23d7066f-ee02-59e9-ae85-3a1372e71eea" :step/math-academy-id 3049 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139376}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139376 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138442 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138314 :question/id #uuid "638af342-1995-5403-84bd-b6c720cb432d" :question/math-academy-id "e-907"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4b91363-1cac-5495-b29b-c14236bc4de6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049502} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049689} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050282}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138802} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139084}] :knowledge-point/title "Performing a Unit Conversion: Converting a Numerator"} :step/id #uuid "48400771-1498-544e-a6cb-80f32c6689d9" :step/math-academy-id 3050 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139377}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139377 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138443 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138315 :question/id #uuid "08aa3547-cb51-5d00-8cb7-3e1a9bd4a695" :question/math-academy-id "e-908"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f10e8464-e555-5358-b97f-230933822fa1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138798} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138799}] :knowledge-point/title "Performing a Unit Conversion: Converting a Denominator"} :step/id #uuid "16237576-82b8-5b51-891e-bf6a4b793259" :step/math-academy-id 3053 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139378}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139378 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138444 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138316 :question/id #uuid "79f9c66b-2e4e